Determine errors in the following statements of Java programs and correct them:
(iii)
int x[5] = {6, -2, 2, 3, 5, 6};
for (int i = 0; i <= 5; i++) {
    System.out.println(x[i]);
}

questions.solution:
Error: int x[5] = {...} is not allowed; the size cannot be written in the declaration (and 6 values are listed anyway).
Correction:
int x[] = {6, -2, 2, 3, 5, 6};
for (int i = 0; i < x.length; i++) {
    System.out.println(x[i]);
}
With 6 elements the indices are 0 to 5, so the loop i <= 5 is then also fine. (The book's version changes the loop to i < 5, which compiles but skips the last element 6.)

